{
  "information": {
    "country": "LT",
    "model_target": "euromod://LT/ConstDef_lt/def_const/$MMS",
    "spine_order": "3",
    "value_type": "scalar",
    "unit": "currency/month",
    "threshold_unit": null,
    "label": {
      "en": "Gross minimum monthly salary: tscsepi, tscsehl and tscer"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$MMS"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "$MMS is Lithuania's gross statutory minimum monthly salary (MMA), currently EUR 1,223.33/month; per its label it also underpins social-insurance-contribution policies outside this batch (tscsepi, tscsehl, tscer). Within these policies it sets the constant-part base of the unemployment benefit formula in bunct_lt/bunct_FYA_lt (ArithOp formula, alongside $bunct_const_rate), and it defines the \"at least two-thirds of the MMS\" earnings/self-employment eligibility floor for the social assistance benefit in bsa00_lt and its bsa_FYA_lt counterpart (Elig_Cond, \"lower limits applied on employment and self-employment income\"; BenCalc Comp_Cond for recipients who become employed), matching the bsa00 Country Report's eligibility condition on employment or self-employment income relative to the MMS. It is also used to derive the $mc_max wage-compensation constant in ConstDef_lt and to gate eligibility in the TransLMA_lt add-on (Elig_Cond, \"MC_EE: step 1\")."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Pension age, MMS, AMS, AMSp,  BSA, SSI, CYI, CBN, basic/asistance pensions bases, RP"
    },
    "last_confirmed_valid_on": null,
    "temporal_basis": "in_force"
  },
